Benign keratosis-like lesions often appear as well-demarcated, "stuck-on" plaques with variable pigmentation from light tan to dark brown or black, showing milia-like cysts, comedo-like openings, fissures and ridges, and occasional hairpin vessels.
Benign keratosis-like lesions often appear as well-demarcated, “stuck-on” brown to black plaques with a rough, verrucous surface; dermoscopy shows milia-like cysts, comedo-like openings, fissures and ridges, variable pigmentation and occasional hairpin vessels.
appears as a well‑circumscribed, "stuck‑on" plaque with uneven waxy surface, ranging light tan to dark brown; dermoscopy reveals milia‑like cysts, comedo‑like openings, fissures, ridges, superficial scaling and sparse dotted vessels.
Benign keratosis-like lesions on dermoscopy appear as well-demarcated, often round or oval brown to black macules or plaques with surface fissures/ridges, milia-like cysts, comedo-like openings, variable scaling, and patterns from flat to verrucous.
shows well-demarcated, stuck-on brown to tan papules with a cerebriform surface of fissures and ridges, scattered white-yellow milia-like cysts and dark comedo-like openings, variable pigmentation intensity and occasional hairpin vessels.
Dermoscopic image shows a well-demarcated, stuck-on plaque with warty surface, variable pigmentation from light tan to dark brown, sharp fissures and ridges, milia-like white cysts, comedo-like openings, and scattered linear vessels (variation 6).
appears as a sharply demarcated, stuck-on brown plaque with cerebriform fissures and ridges, scattered milia-like cysts or comedo-like openings, variable dark pigment clods and occasional hairpin or dotted vessels on dermoscopy.
Dermoscopic image shows a sharply demarcated, rough, stuck-on plaque with heterogeneous brown to tan pigmentation, moth-eaten border, multiple milia-like cysts and comedo-like openings, superficial scale, fissures, and occasional hairpin or dotted vessels.
In dermoscopy, benign keratosis-like lesions appear as sharply demarcated, stuck-on plaques with variable pigmentation from light brown to black, exhibiting milia-like cysts, comedo-like openings, fissures and ridges, moth-eaten borders, and occasional hairpin vessels.
shows sharply demarcated, stuck-on appearing brown to black papules and plaques with variable pigmentation, surface keratotic scale, milia-like cysts or comedo-like openings, fissured or brain-like ridges, and occasional focal hemorrhage.
